@startuml 00-overall-migration-flow-academic-boxed
title QEMU Live Migration — Adaptive Per-Channel XBZRLE Architecture
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantFontStyle bold
autonumber
!pragma teoz true

' --- ACADEMIC GRAPHITE PALETTE ---
skinparam Sequence {
    LifeLineBorderColor #444444
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F0F0F0
    ArrowColor #1A365D
    ActorBorderColor #1A365D
    GroupBorderColor #A0AEC0
    GroupHeaderFontColor #2D3748
    GroupBackgroundColor #F7FAFC
}
skinparam Note {
    BackgroundColor #F7FAFC
    BorderColor #CBD5E0
    FontColor #2D3748
}

' === SOURCE HOST BOXES ===
box "QEMU Source" #Lavender
    box "Kernel" #F8FAFC
        participant KVM as "Dirty-log Driver\n(KVM Interface)" #E6F0FA
    end box
    box "Mainline Migration Engine" #EDF2F7
        participant Engine      as "Core Migration\nController" #E6F0FA
        participant Sync        as "Bitmap\nSynchronizer" #E6F0FA
        participant Scanner     as "Page Scanner\n& Router" #E6F0FA
        participant Sender      as "Channel Worker\n(Sender Thread)" #E6F0FA
    end box

    box "Our Proposed Modules" #FFF2CC
        participant HotMap      as "Page Hotness\nTracker" #FFE6CC
        participant Encoder     as "XBZRLE Delta\nEncoder" #FFE6CC
    end box
end box

' === NETWORK ===
participant Network as "TCP Network\nChannels" #E2E8F0

' === DESTINATION HOST BOXES ===
box "QEMU Destination" #Lavender
    box "Mainline Process" #EDF2F7
        participant Receiver    as "Channel Worker\n(Receiver Thread)" #E6F0FA
        participant GuestRAM    as "Destination\nGuest RAM" #E6F0FA
    end box
    
    box "Our Proposed Modules" #FFF2CC
        participant Decoder     as "XBZRLE Delta\nDecoder" #FFE6CC
    end box
end box
' ==========================================
' == DIAGRAM FLOW ==
' ==========================================

== Phase 1: Periodic Bitmap Synchronization ==

Engine --> Engine : migration_thread loop triggers period
Engine -> Sync : migration_bitmap_sync()
Sync -> KVM : memory_global_dirty_log_sync()
KVM --> Sync : Return kernel dirty bitmap bitmask

Sync -> Sync : ramblock_sync_dirty_bitmap()\nUpdate master migration bitmap

group #FFF9E6 Proposed: Dynamic Hotness Mapping
    Sync -> HotMap : Sync dirty bits to hotness matrix
    note over HotMap
        **Tracking Mechanism:**
        Increments frequency counter per dirty page (max 3),
        decrements on clean rounds (min 0).
    end note
    HotMap --> Sync : Dynamic map updated
end

Sync --> Engine : Synchronization cycle complete

== Phase 2: Driven Page Routing ==

Engine -> Scanner : Scan dirty pages in master bitmap

group #FFF9E6 Proposed: Content-Aware Scheduling
    note over Scanner
        **Adaptive Routing Strategy:**
        Queries HotMap to bind frequently modified 
        pages to a dedicated hot thread.
    end note
    
    alt hot_page_is_hot(page) == true
        Scanner -> Sender : Dispatch to **Thread 0**\n(Dedicated Hot-Channel)
    else cold page
        Scanner -> Sender : Dispatch to **Thread [1 ... N-1]**\n(Load-balanced via GPA hash)
    end
end

== Phase 3: Distributed Delta Coding & Transmission ==

Sender -> Encoder : Initiate batch encoding pipeline
note over Encoder
  **Lockless Design:** Each worker maintains an independent 
  PageCache to eliminate thread contention.
end note

loop For each page within the current batch
    group #FFF9E6 Proposed: Isolated Differential Coding
        alt Page Cache HIT
            Encoder -> Encoder : Compute XOR(new, cached_old)\nGenerate differential metadata\nSet flags (delta_encoded = 1)
        else Page Cache MISS
            Encoder -> Encoder : Commit full page to local cache\nSet flags (delta_encoded = 0)
        end
    end
end

Encoder -> Network : Transmit MultiFDPacket\n(Metadata Header + Payload Buffer)

== Phase 4: Destination Reconstruction ==

Network -> Receiver : Ingest stream payload via per-channel socket
Receiver -> Decoder : Submit batch for processing

loop For each page within the current batch
    group #FFF9E6 Proposed: Parallel Reconstruction
        alt delta_encoded == 1
            Decoder -> Decoder : Retrieve baseline from receiver cache\nApply XOR delta -> Reconstruct runtime state
        else delta_encoded == 0
            Decoder -> Decoder : Write full page direct to receiver cache
        end
    end
end

Decoder -> GuestRAM : Write finalized page to target memory space

@enduml
